     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is well above the maximum, and I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for XR), and usually no more than 1,000 mg in a single dose.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about twice the daily maximum. Even with normal renal function, it substantially raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThis may be a transposition or unit error. Some possibilities:\n\n- **850 mg three times daily:** 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total:** for example, 850 mg twice daily.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily:** 2,000 mg/day.\n\nPlease tell me the intended dose, or confirm that 1700 mg TID is deliberate. If it is, I'll need that confirmation stated explicitly, and I'd suggest documenting the rationale. Once I have the corrected dose, I'll enter it as metformin PO with meals, with the frequency and formulation (IR or XR) you specify.\n\nI also don't have an order-entry tool connected in this session, so I can prepare the order text but can't submit it to the EHR myself."
     }
