    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\nFirst, I have no order-entry tool connected in this session, so I couldn't submit anything to the EHR regardless. Second, 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and there's no indication where it's appropriate. Glycemic benefit plateaus around 2,000 mg/day, so the extra drug adds lactic acidosis and GI toxicity risk without added efficacy. I'd rather not prepare an order I believe could seriously harm the patient.\n\nYou are the prescriber, and this is your decision. If you place it yourself, expect pharmacy verification to flag or reject it, and a hard-stop dose alert may require an override with documented rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n\n- Draft the order at a maximum-dose alternative for you to review, such as metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, immediate-release).\n- Draft a pharmacy consult note if you have a specific clinical reason for exceeding the limit and want it reviewed.\n- Suggest add-on agents if the goal is greater glycemic control than metformin alone can give.\n\nLet me know which you'd like."
     }
